      "evidence": "The title calls this “A surrogate loss that does not control task cost.” The dependency definition says, “An expert surrogate loss is a function ℓ:S×K→[0,1] satisfying ℓ(s,θ)≥e(s,θ) for every s∈S and θ∈K.” Here the learner always chooses b while the expert chooses a*, so e(s,θ)=1, but ℓ=0; the Example itself says the score “fails the required disagreement-domination condition.” Thus this score is not an expert surrogate under the library’s definition, despite the title.",
